window.docContents[96].resolve({"/releases/#release-v4___36___0":{"contents":"\n\n* Breaking change: Manual title pages and chapters rendered on separate pages now carry their registered section IDs as the id attribute of their headings, so links to these sections resolve correctly.\nThe document title in single-page output also carries its ID. (#983)* In the Manual genre, there is a new entry point for metaprograms that elaborate inline Lean code called elabInlineLean.\nIt runs an elaborator action in the scope that the document's Lean code has established, passes the section variables to the action, and arranges for the unused variable linter not to emit spurious warnings for binders in the code.\nFor code that does not need to re-establish the saved scope, the new helper withInlineLeanInfoTree correctly saves info trees.\n (#1062)* Breaking change: Verso now uses the Lean types and custom HTML syntax provided by Lean, rather than its own implementation of a custom HTML syntax. (#974, #987)* Breaking change: Verso markup is parsed by code that is part of Lean.\nThe upstream parser was rewritten to enable code formatting, with substantial improvements to error messages along the way.\nAdapting to the new parser required changes in Verso. (#989)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Writing Documentation in Lean with Verso\u0009Release Notes","header":"Verso 4.36.0 (in development)","id":"/releases/#release-v4___36___0"}});